.TH PRIVACITY 1 "2026-06" "privacity" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
privacity \- VPN Gate auto-connector
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B privacity
[\fB\-c\fR \fIcountry\fR] [\fB\-\-country\fR \fIcountry\fR]
[\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetches the fastest public VPN Gate servers and connects via OpenVPN
\-\- interactive or daemon mode.  Picks the server with the highest
score, sanitizes its OpenVPN config, and handles the full connection
lifecycle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-country\fR \fIcountry\fR
Filter servers by country name or code (e.g. "Japan", "US", "Korea").
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B privacity
Interactive guided mode (default).  Shows top 3 servers, asks for
confirmation, then connects and displays live speed, IP, and ping.
Press \fBQ\fR to disconnect, \fBS\fR to switch server.
.TP
.B daemon
Connect in background.  No terminal needed after connection.
.TP
.B daemon \-\-persist
Install systemd user service so the VPN auto-connects after login.
.TP
.B daemon \-\-unpersist
Remove the systemd user service.
.TP
.B list
Show top 10 servers and list available countries.
.TP
.B disconnect
Tear down the current VPN connection.
.TP
.B reconnect
Pick the best server (optionally filtered by \fB\-c\fR) and reconnect.
.TP
.B status
Show current connection: server, country, external IP, ping, speed.
.TP
.B speedtest
Measure download speed via Cloudflare and print result in Mbps.
.TP
.B update
Pull the latest version from git and reinstall.
.TP
.B help
Show the help message with all commands and options.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/privacity/config\fR
Configuration file.  Format: \fBKEY=VALUE\fR.
Supported keys: \fBcountry\fR, \fBmode\fR (daemon|interactive).
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/servers.csv\fR
Cached VPN Gate server list (5 minute TTL).
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/active.ovpn\fR
Sanitized OpenVPN config of the active connection.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/privacity.pid\fR
PID of the background OpenVPN process.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/last_host\fR
Last connected server hostname and country.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/openvpn.log\fR
OpenVPN daemon log.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Connect to the best server (interactive)
.B privacity
.TP
Connect to a Japanese server in background
.B privacity \-c Japan daemon
.TP
List Korean servers
.B privacity \-c Korea list
.TP
Check current connection
.B privacity status
.TP
Reconnect to a US server
.B privacity \-c US reconnect
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Runtime: openvpn, wget, curl, base64 (coreutils), sudo.
